00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:20,320
Right?

221
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:23,200
Like, I talk to a lot of believers that feel guilty about being tempted.

222
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,440
They feel bad.

223
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:25,380
They feel defeated.

224
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:26,660
They're like, I'm tempted to do this.

225
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:27,440
I'm tempted to do that.

226
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:30,980
I feel like I'm a bad Christian or something like that.

227
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,600
Temptation happens to all of us.

228
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:35,320
Temptation is not a sin.

229
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:41,080
But we pay attention to temptation because temptation can very quickly and easily lead us into sin.

230
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:43,580
So don't feel guilty about being tempted.

231
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:51,540
But when you are tempted, pay attention to that temptation and see what is it that your desires are telling you.

232
00:16:52,780 --> 00:17:01,680
Ultimately, desires aren't always bad, but how we choose to satisfy those desires, determine whether or not it's sin or not.

233
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:06,580
Jeremiah 17, verse 9, again, consider the source.

234
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:10,280
The human heart is the most deceitful of all things.

235
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,180
It is desperately wicked.

236
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:13,840
Who really knows how bad it is?

237
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:17,340
And so when we have desires, we just have to consider the source.

238
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:27,540
We have to acknowledge that our desires are coming from within us, and within us is a heart that is deceitful and wicked, and that can lead us astray.

239
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:33,560
That can lead us down a path that does not lead to life or flourishing that God has designed.

240
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:35,700
So James says, consider the source.

241
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:36,520
It's not from God.

242
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:38,000
It's from your desires.

243
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:47,200
Again, your desires aren't always bad, but oftentimes your sinful heart tells you to satisfy those desires in a way that goes against God.

244
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:48,520
It's designed.

245
00:17:48,520 --> 00:18:07,960
So there's this period of time I think we see in the text that's not really clear, but I think we can parse it out, is in between desire and disobedience is this piece that is deception.

246
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:19,880
So in between we have this desire, there's this temptation, and then before the temptation turns to sin, there's this deception where we believe a lie about the desire.

247
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:22,880
Again, because not all desires are sinful.

248
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:32,520
Desires often times have good satisfactions, good things that God designed for those desires to be satisfied with.

249
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:44,580
But between, if we're not paying attention, if we're not careful, that desire, our sinful heart can lie to us and tell us that we can fulfill that desire in a way that goes against God's design.

250
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:47,520
I love how Pastor Vance Pittman puts it.

251
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:47,820
He says,

252
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:58,340
All temptation is rooted in the lie that something other than God and his will can meet my needs and satisfy my desires.

253
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:02,680
All temptation is rooted in the lie, the deception, right?

254
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:06,080
There's a deception between our desires and our disobedience.

255
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:17,320
In the moment when we're tempted, we have to pay attention to what we're thinking about that temptation, that desire, because there are godly ways that we can satisfy that desire, and there are sinful ways.

256
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:26,040
And ultimately, the lie, the deception, that God or something other than God or his will can satisfy those desires.

257
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,900
That's where the sin comes into our life.

258
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:35,200
In between our desires and our disobedience is the playing ground where sin happens.

259
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:39,720
