00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:41,800
Like, I got a couple illustrations I want to draw.

261
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:43,320
Number one, hungry.

262
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:44,780
Being hungry is a desire.

263
00:19:44,780 --> 00:19:49,840
Is that a sinful desire that you have, like being hungry, wanting food?

264
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:51,380
That's not a sinful desire, right?

265
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:55,640
There's plenty of godly ways to satisfy the desire of being hungry.

266
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:57,720
That wouldn't be disobedient.

267
00:19:57,720 --> 00:19:59,460
That wouldn't lead to death or destruction.

268
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:17,320
But eating a 12-pack of tacos and a large Baja Blast at midnight on a regular basis might be considered an unhealthy decision and not stewarding God's resources well, not stewarding the body that you've been given well.

269
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:25,820
So, there's a desire and there's good ways to fulfill that desire and unhealthy ways that ultimately, you know, you do it once or twice, not a big deal.

270
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:39,160
But you spend, those of us that have been in college who lived off of McDoubles and McChickens and combining the two at midnight might not be the healthiest way to steward the resources that God has given you.

271
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:42,860
Being angry, listen to this, being angry about an injustice at work.

272
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:45,180
