But if you allow that anger to turn into bitterness, and that bitterness drives you to gossip and slander behind other people's backs, that is disobedience.

280
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:23,800
That is where that desire for justice, and there's a righteous way to fulfill that desire.

281
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:33,200
But if you're not careful, if you let bitterness and angriness grow in your heart, you can very easily turn that desire into disobedience because you're believing a lie.

282
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:37,520
You're believing that you can satisfy that desire apart from God's will.

283
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:39,340
God's will is that justice happens.

284
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:44,780
God's will is not that you go behind people's backs in anger and slander and bitterness and gossip.

285
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:52,240
Like, there is healthy and righteous ways to address the desire, and there are unhealthy, sinful ways that ultimately lead to destruction.

286
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:59,080
Wanting to enjoy an evening of fellowship around the fire with some drinks is a desire.

287
00:21:59,580 --> 00:22:05,460
But after a few, when you decide that you deserve a few more, because after all, you've worked really hard.

288
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:09,940
You've been really stressed, and you deserve an opportunity to unwind.

289
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:16,060
That desire, there's deception that is bred between desire and disobedience.

290
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:21,420
And you tell yourself that you deserve something that is outside of God's designs for your life.

291
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:25,380
The desire for sex inside of marriage is a good desire.

292
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:35,800
But when you decide, it would be easier for you to satisfy that desire behind a computer screen instead of taking time to invest in the relationship with your spouse that God has created you for.

293
00:22:36,300 --> 00:22:45,120
That would lead to true, soul-satisfying intimacy, that is deception between desire and disobedience.

294
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:53,480
When you begin to believe the lie, that there are other ways to satisfy the desire outside of God's design, that's the playing ground.

295
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:59,240
When we move from just this desire, this temptation, to this disobedience.

296
00:22:59,240 --> 00:23:02,720
See, there's a negative outcome to temptations.

297
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:04,980
It's disobedience that leads to destruction.

298
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:11,060
And so when we're tempted, when our desires show up, we pay attention to what we're telling ourselves about those desires.

299
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:15,320
Is there a healthy, God-honoring way to satisfy these desires?

300
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:20,040
If not, we need to pay attention to those things.

301
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:27,160
In what ways are we being drawn away, enticed out of that desire into disobedience?

302
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:32,140
The language that James uses there is actually that of like a fishing lure, right?

303
00:23:32,140 --> 00:23:34,880
Like it's like this fake thing that looks real.

304
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:40,800
It's like this fake thing that looks like it's going to ultimately satisfy you, but you know deep down inside it will not.

305
00:23:42,180 --> 00:23:47,360
So, James is saying temptation starts with your desire.

306
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:57,800
And if you're not careful, your desire can be lied to, to believe that there's another way to satisfy that desire outside of God's design.

307
00:23:57,800 --> 00:24:06,180
And when your desire is deceived, it brings forth sin, and sin ultimately brings forth destruction.

308
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:16,740
So, I don't know if any of you Bible scholars in the room noticed this yet or not, but James is retracing the first sin.

309
00:24:16,740 --> 00:24:20,360
He's retracing the experience that Adam and Eve had in the garden.

310
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:26,200
He's saying the first sin, the first temptation that led to sin, that ultimately led to destruction,

311
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:33,940
is a pattern for how every other temptation happens from the moment that Adam and Eve first sinned until the moment that Jesus returns again.

312
00:24:33,940 --> 00:24:38,640
All of our temptations follow the same desire that Adam and Eve had in the garden.

313
00:24:38,640 --> 00:24:41,400
See, Eve, she had a desire.

314
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:45,120
She saw that the fruit was pleasing to the eye.

315
00:24:46,500 --> 00:24:48,140
And was that desire bad?

316
00:24:48,140 --> 00:24:51,080
Was it bad to look upon the fruit that God had created and said,

317
00:24:51,080 --> 00:24:54,100
that fruit looks beautiful, that fruit looks good?

318
00:24:54,100 --> 00:24:56,360
No, that desire is not a sin.

