00:24:56,360 --> 00:24:59,840
But God had said very clearly, this one fruit, it's off limits.

320
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:00,500
Don't touch it.

321
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:03,640
Don't eat of it or you will surely die.

322
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:04,820
And so she had a desire.

323
00:25:04,820 --> 00:25:07,640
The desire in and of itself wasn't bad.

324
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:13,340
But in the moment of her desire, the enemy shows up and deceives her.

325
00:25:13,340 --> 00:25:16,420
He says, you won't surely die.

326
00:25:16,420 --> 00:25:24,040
So in the moment between her desire and her disobedience, she's surrounded in a beautiful garden with every fruit tree you could ever imagine.

327
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:28,820
And God says, taste and eat, enjoy all of the good things except for this one fruit.

328
00:25:28,820 --> 00:25:29,760
Just this one fruit.

329
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:30,400
Don't eat of it.

330
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:30,940
Trust me.

331
00:25:30,940 --> 00:25:31,720
Believe me.

332
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:34,140
Because if you eat of it, it will lead to death.

333
00:25:34,140 --> 00:25:38,960
Just believe that I have good plans for you, that I have a good life designed for you.

334
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:39,940
Just listen to me.

335
00:25:39,940 --> 00:25:41,060
And she has this desire.

336
00:25:41,060 --> 00:25:42,320
That tree looks good, though.

337
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:46,020
And then in that desire, she's deceived.

338
00:25:46,020 --> 00:25:47,640
She's told a lie.

339
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:49,220
You won't surely die.

340
00:25:49,220 --> 00:25:56,320
And so then Adam and Eve believe the lie that that desire could be satisfied outside of God's plan for their life.

341
00:25:56,320 --> 00:25:57,260
And they disobey.

342
00:25:57,260 --> 00:26:00,660
And that disobedience led to destruction.

343
00:26:01,380 --> 00:26:06,320
And since that day, every temptation that we face follows that same pattern.

344
00:26:06,320 --> 00:26:07,560
We have a desire.

345
00:26:07,560 --> 00:26:18,780
And there's a time in between our desire and our disobedience where we can either believe God's word and find a way to satisfy the desires that honor God.

346
00:26:18,780 --> 00:26:23,720
Or we can be deceived into believing that there's a better way to satisfy our desires.

347
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:28,780
That we can satisfy our desires outside of God's plan for our life.

348
00:26:28,780 --> 00:26:37,440
And in between the desire and the disobedience is the ground in which we decide whether we're going to obey or disobey.

349
00:26:37,440 --> 00:26:41,160
Whether we're going to believe truth or we're going to believe a lie.

350
00:26:42,740 --> 00:26:50,120
So, James is saying, when desire comes about, pay attention to that desire.

351
00:26:50,120 --> 00:26:57,680
Look for ways in which you can satisfy that desire in a way that honors God.

352
00:27:00,460 --> 00:27:08,200
The root of every deception between our desires and our disobedience is the lie that God isn't good.

