00:32:23,680 --> 00:32:26,540
Don't worry about how this will affect your life.

439
00:32:26,540 --> 00:32:30,120
My bed is spread with beautiful blankets, colorful sheets, Egyptian linen.

440
00:32:30,120 --> 00:32:32,740
I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloe, cinnamon.

441
00:32:32,740 --> 00:32:37,020
Come, let us drink, and let us have a fill of our love until morning.

442
00:32:37,020 --> 00:32:39,280
Let us enjoy each other's caresses.

443
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:41,100
For my husband, he's not home.

444
00:32:41,100 --> 00:32:42,280
He's away on a long trip.

445
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:44,480
He's not coming back for a while.

446
00:32:44,480 --> 00:32:51,680
So, she seduced him with her pretty speech and enticed him away with her flattery, with her deception.

447
00:32:54,160 --> 00:33:00,520
And this is a perfect illustration of what we do, how we often wrongly handle temptation.

448
00:33:00,520 --> 00:33:01,460
Right?

449
00:33:01,460 --> 00:33:04,640
We're like, oh, I'm just going to dabble with it.

450
00:33:04,640 --> 00:33:06,600
I'm just going to hang out with it.

451
00:33:06,600 --> 00:33:08,780
It's not going to cause that much problems.

452
00:33:08,780 --> 00:33:11,200
I'm just going to go for a walk down by the immoral woman's house.

453
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:12,180
I'm not going to talk to her.

454
00:33:12,180 --> 00:33:13,380
I won't even look at her.

455
00:33:13,820 --> 00:33:14,900
I'll keep my head down.

456
00:33:14,900 --> 00:33:15,780
I'll just enjoy the walk.

457
00:33:15,780 --> 00:33:27,080
And then over that entire story, he had time after time after time where he could have snapped out of it and said, no, this is outside of God's design for my life.

458
00:33:27,080 --> 00:33:33,260
Yes, my desires might be satisfied in the moment, but this is disobedience that's going to lead me through destruction.

459
00:33:33,260 --> 00:33:40,000
And time after time, he had that window, that pocket of time where he was getting sucked in and sucked in and sucked in.

460
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:44,360
And all he had to do was snap out of it and say, no, this is against God's plan for my life.

461
00:33:44,360 --> 00:33:46,040
God has a better plan for my life.

462
00:33:46,040 --> 00:33:49,540
And we've all seen ourselves do this.

463
00:33:49,540 --> 00:33:54,100
Time and time again, the deception starts small and it gets worse and worse.

464
00:33:54,160 --> 00:34:00,800
And we justify it because we have a desire that we want to be satisfied and we don't care if it leads to disobedience.

465
00:34:00,800 --> 00:34:06,260
The lies we tell ourselves in between desire and disobedience are, it's not that big of a deal.

466
00:34:06,260 --> 00:34:09,220
It's not going to hurt anyone.

467
00:34:09,220 --> 00:34:11,860
I've been through a lot.

468
00:34:11,860 --> 00:34:13,180
I deserve this.

469
00:34:13,180 --> 00:34:15,580
Does God really care about this?

470
00:34:15,580 --> 00:34:18,000
No one is going to find out.

471
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:23,080
The immediate benefit far outweighs my inevitable consequences.

472
00:34:23,320 --> 00:34:26,000
James is saying, follow Jesus.

473
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:26,820
Pay attention.

474
00:34:26,820 --> 00:34:29,400
Sin hides its consequences.

475
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:34,040
Sin deceives you in the moment between desire and disobedience.

476
00:34:34,040 --> 00:34:39,440
It's lying to you and trying to get you to believe that God does not have a good plan for your life.

477
00:34:39,440 --> 00:34:48,400
And I know, I know stories in this room of people, testimonies that would say, I never intended to end up where I ended up.

478
00:34:48,400 --> 00:34:51,420
I didn't think that it was going to be that big of a deal in the moment.

479
00:34:51,540 --> 00:34:54,000
I didn't think that it was going to hurt anyone.

480
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:58,320
But James is saying, listen, temptation is nothing to play with.

481
00:34:58,320 --> 00:35:02,680
Because temptation drags you away to disobedience.

482
00:35:02,680 --> 00:35:06,220
And disobedience drags you away to destruction.

483
00:35:06,220 --> 00:35:16,520
So look, I know up until this point that this is a pretty heavy message for us.

484
00:35:16,520 --> 00:35:19,140
It's a pretty heavy message for me.

485
00:35:19,140 --> 00:35:23,840
Because there's a lot of us in the room where we've had some big failures in our life.

486
00:35:23,840 --> 00:35:30,800
Like some of you right now are thinking about times in which you allowed deception to breed lies in your life.

487
00:35:30,800 --> 00:35:34,280
And you allowed your life to go down a path that you never would have intended for yourself.

488
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:35,920
And there's guilt and shame there.

489
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:43,300
And some of us, we're just in this cycle of shame where we've just failed so many times that we identify by that sin.

490
00:35:43,300 --> 00:35:44,060
We're like, you know what?

491
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:47,300
I'm stuck in this pattern of sin and I'm never going to get out.

492
00:35:47,300 --> 00:35:49,560
And we have shame and guilt.

493
00:35:49,560 --> 00:35:52,100
But I have good news for you this morning.

494
00:35:52,100 --> 00:36:00,900
See, James and all of the writers of Scripture are clear that Satan, he came to steal, kill, and destroy.

495
00:36:01,060 --> 00:36:05,380
But Jesus, Jesus has come to bring life.

496
00:36:05,380 --> 00:36:09,840
James is saying, how do we defeat temptation?

497
00:36:09,840 --> 00:36:11,520
Look at verse 16.

498
00:36:11,520 --> 00:36:13,540
He says, don't be misled.

499
00:36:13,540 --> 00:36:15,260
Don't believe a lie.

500
00:36:15,260 --> 00:36:22,280
Whatever is good and is perfect, it's a gift coming down to us from God the Father who created all the lights in heaven.

501
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:24,460
He never changes or casts a shifting shadow.

502
00:36:24,460 --> 00:36:31,200
So he chose to give birth to us by giving us his true word and we, out of all creation, became his prized possession.

503
00:36:31,200 --> 00:36:37,240
He's saying, Satan, the world, the flesh, they all have a plan for our desire.

504
00:36:37,240 --> 00:36:42,100
And that plan is to lead us to a place where they can steal, kill, and destroy from our life.

505
00:36:42,100 --> 00:36:44,960
But Jesus, Jesus came to give us life.

506
00:36:44,960 --> 00:36:46,700
Matthew chapter 4.

507
00:36:49,320 --> 00:36:56,060
James is rehearsing how the temptation worked for Adam and Eve in the garden.

508
00:36:56,060 --> 00:36:59,780
And how every temptation since then works.

509
00:36:59,780 --> 00:37:02,380
Desire leads to deception.

510
00:37:02,380 --> 00:37:04,640
Deception leads to disobedience.

511
00:37:04,640 --> 00:37:07,220
Disobedience leads to destruction.

512
00:37:07,220 --> 00:37:11,100
But there was one man.

513
00:37:11,100 --> 00:37:13,340
His name was Jesus.

514
00:37:14,420 --> 00:37:21,060
And in Matthew chapter 4, it says this, that Jesus was led by the Spirit into the wilderness to be what?

515
00:37:21,060 --> 00:37:22,420
Tempted.

516
00:37:22,420 --> 00:37:26,600
Jesus was led in the wilderness to be tempted there by the devil.

517
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:29,640
For 40 days and 40 nights, Jesus fasted.

518
00:37:29,640 --> 00:37:30,980
He became very hungry.

519
00:37:30,980 --> 00:37:33,700
And during that time, the devil came and they said to him,

520
00:37:33,700 --> 00:37:39,620
If you are the Son of God, tell these stones to become loaves of bread.

521
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:43,560
So we've got Adam and Eve in a perfect garden.

522
00:37:43,560 --> 00:37:45,920
With everything going right for them.

523
00:37:45,920 --> 00:37:50,080
With God providing everything that they could ever need or imagine.

524
00:37:50,080 --> 00:37:52,300
And then, in that moment, there's a desire.

525
00:37:52,300 --> 00:37:55,660
And Satan shows up and deceives and lies.

526
00:37:55,660 --> 00:37:57,980
He seeks to steal, kill, and destroy.

527
00:37:57,980 --> 00:37:59,480
And he says, God's not good.

528
00:37:59,480 --> 00:38:01,800
God's trying to keep something good from you.

529
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:03,740
You won't surely die if you eat that fruit.

530
00:38:03,740 --> 00:38:06,460
And they believed that lie.

531
00:38:06,460 --> 00:38:08,940
Their desire.

532
00:38:09,400 --> 00:38:10,720
In their desire, they were deceived.

533
00:38:10,720 --> 00:38:12,160
In their deception, they sinned.

534
00:38:12,160 --> 00:38:14,260
In their sin, it led to destruction.

535
00:38:14,260 --> 00:38:18,140
But then, God sent his Son, Jesus.

536
00:38:18,140 --> 00:38:21,000
Who in, not a garden, but in a desert.

537
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:22,500
Starving.

538
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:24,700
40 days of no food.

539
00:38:24,700 --> 00:38:25,580
Hungry.

540
00:38:25,580 --> 00:38:26,840
He had a desire.

541
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:27,860
Hunger.

542
00:38:27,860 --> 00:38:30,400
And Satan came and said,

543
00:38:30,400 --> 00:38:33,800
You can fulfill that desire apart from God's plan for your life.

544
00:38:33,800 --> 00:38:35,600
Just, you're the Son of God.

545
00:38:35,600 --> 00:38:38,000
Just turn that stone into bread.

546
00:38:38,100 --> 00:38:39,420
And what does Jesus do?

547
00:38:39,420 --> 00:38:45,060
In the moment between his desire and his disobedience, he speaks truth to it.

548
00:38:45,060 --> 00:38:48,020
He says, no.

549
00:38:48,020 --> 00:38:55,640
The Scriptures say, people do not live by bread alone, but by every word that comes from the mouth of God.

550
00:38:55,640 --> 00:39:03,160
See, in a moment of extreme desire, Jesus was tempted to satisfy his desires apart from God.

551
00:39:03,220 --> 00:39:11,540
But in that moment, in that moment where he felt the pull, the draw between his desire, he felt a draw.

552
00:39:11,540 --> 00:39:13,240
He acknowledged it.

553
00:39:13,240 --> 00:39:13,960
And he says, no.

554
00:39:13,960 --> 00:39:16,600
No, I'm going to trust God's word.

555
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:19,540
I'm going to believe that God has a better plan for my life.

556
00:39:19,540 --> 00:39:22,720
He chose to believe that God's way is better.

557
00:39:22,720 --> 00:39:26,460
See, Jesus has succeeded in every way that we have failed.

558
00:39:26,820 --> 00:39:51,420
See, we have all failed in this.

559
00:39:51,420 --> 00:39:59,260
All of us, we've had a desire, and we've believed a lie about that desire, and we've sought to find satisfaction in our lives apart from God.

560
00:40:00,160 --> 00:40:06,220
But one man entered a desert, was tempted in the same way that we were tempted.

561
00:40:06,220 --> 00:40:10,240
And yet, he succeeded in every way in which we have failed.

562
00:40:10,240 --> 00:40:15,740
And because of that, listen, brothers and sisters, because of that, you do not have to be perfect at defeating temptation.

563
00:40:15,740 --> 00:40:18,520
Jesus did that for you.

564
00:40:20,720 --> 00:40:26,640
But, you can consistently have victory over temptation because Jesus has showed you the way.

565
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:34,360
When in your desire, you're tempted to believe a lie about that desire, call it out.

566
00:40:34,360 --> 00:40:35,240
Speak truth to it.

567
00:40:35,240 --> 00:40:38,720
Remind yourself that God is good and that he has a good plan for your life.

568
00:40:38,720 --> 00:40:42,400
See, Jesus has secured your final victory.

569
00:40:43,500 --> 00:40:47,280
And he has given you the Holy Spirit to strengthen you for your current victory.

570
00:40:47,280 --> 00:40:55,940
There is a negative consequence, a negative outcome to temptation if we allow ourselves to be lied to.

571
00:40:55,940 --> 00:41:04,620
And if we're going to run the race faithfully, if we're going to finish our lives and receive that crown of life for finishing the race,

572
00:41:04,620 --> 00:41:10,660
we're going to be a people that learn to embrace trials and avoid temptation.

573
00:41:10,940 --> 00:41:12,020
We're not going to be perfect at it.

574
00:41:12,020 --> 00:41:14,360
We're going to fall short day in and day out.

575
00:41:14,360 --> 00:41:17,100
But Jesus was perfect for us.

576
00:41:17,100 --> 00:41:19,460
He secured that victory for us.

577
00:41:19,460 --> 00:41:26,020
And now he's given us the Holy Spirit, given us strength to be able to, in the moment when we are being deceived,

578
00:41:26,020 --> 00:41:28,840
our desires are enticing us away into sin.

579
00:41:28,840 --> 00:41:31,180
We can speak truth to ourselves in that moment.

580
00:41:31,180 --> 00:41:39,780
I love how Paul says that we can take every thought captive when you're being tempted to believe that God is trying to rob you of joy.

581
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:46,220
And you remind yourself that God is good and that he has a better solution to any desire that you might have.

582
00:41:46,220 --> 00:41:53,200
Jesus has secured your final victory and he's given you the Holy Spirit to empower your current victory.

583
00:41:53,200 --> 00:41:55,420
What will we do with that?

584
00:41:57,920 --> 00:42:06,980
Will we pay attention to our desires that are trying to deceive us into disobedience?

585
00:42:06,980 --> 00:42:10,540
Will we remind ourselves that God is good, that he has a good plan for our lives?

586
00:42:10,540 --> 00:42:17,900
Will we allow the enemy to lie to us over and over and over again?

587
00:42:17,920 --> 00:42:24,100
One of my favorite verses in all of the Bibles, in Hebrews chapter 3, says to encourage one another daily,

588
00:42:24,100 --> 00:42:29,300
so that none of you will be hardened by the deceitfulness of sin.

589
00:42:29,300 --> 00:42:34,980
See, there's this thing that happens to us if we're not careful, if we don't pay attention,

590
00:42:36,260 --> 00:42:41,440
that if we believe enough lies, our heart just gets hardened.

591
00:42:41,440 --> 00:42:49,660
We just constantly are living underneath this deception that God isn't good and that he doesn't have a good plan for us.

592
00:42:49,660 --> 00:42:53,240
And in my heart for us, it's not that we'd be perfect.

593
00:42:53,240 --> 00:43:00,940
It's just that we try, that we pay attention, that we would take hold of the victory that Jesus has purchased for us on the cross,

594
00:43:01,060 --> 00:43:08,440
that we would follow his example, that when, in that moment, between his desire and his disobedience,

595
00:43:08,440 --> 00:43:10,400
he chose to speak truth to it.

596
00:43:10,400 --> 00:43:13,100
He chose to believe that God's plan is good.

597
00:43:13,100 --> 00:43:23,940
This week, when you face temptations, when your desire tells you to find satisfaction apart from God's design, God's plan,

598
00:43:23,940 --> 00:43:25,960
and you're like, my prayer is that you speak truth to it.

599
00:43:25,960 --> 00:43:29,300
Jesus quoted Scripture to the enemy.

600
00:43:29,300 --> 00:43:29,920
He says, no.

601
00:43:31,060 --> 00:43:32,280
God's way is better than your way.

602
00:43:32,280 --> 00:43:34,380
Your way leads to death and destruction.

603
00:43:34,380 --> 00:43:37,140
God's way leads to abundant life.

604
00:43:37,140 --> 00:43:42,760
Let us be a people who, in the tension between our desire and our disobedience,

605
00:43:42,760 --> 00:43:45,960
call out the lies and speak truth to it.

606
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:49,900
We obey because Jesus has purchased that victory for us.

607
00:43:49,900 --> 00:43:50,280
Let me pray.

608
00:43:50,280 --> 00:43:56,960
Father, I thank you for Jesus, who succeeded in every way in which we failed,

609
00:43:57,920 --> 00:44:01,140
who was tempted in every way in which we were tempted.

610
00:44:01,140 --> 00:44:05,280
Yet, he did not sin, and he secured for us final victory.

611
00:44:05,280 --> 00:44:11,640
If we would just place our faith and trust in him, we received the victory.

612
00:44:14,200 --> 00:44:17,420
May we have practical, daily victories over temptation.

613
00:44:17,420 --> 00:44:20,300
May we not give in to sin that leads to destruction.

614
00:44:20,300 --> 00:44:23,300
May we be a people that shine the light of Jesus.

615
00:44:23,300 --> 00:44:27,820
That in our temptation, we speak truth.

616
00:44:27,820 --> 00:44:30,960
We believe God is good.

617
00:44:30,960 --> 00:44:36,240
We seek to find a way to satisfy our desires in a way that honors God.

618
00:44:36,240 --> 00:44:37,960
For your glory and for our good.

619
00:44:37,960 --> 00:44:39,520
In Jesus' name I pray.

620
00:44:39,520 --> 00:44:40,300
Amen.
